"""Single-point mutants of experiments/exp_astro_insitu.py, for tools/mutants.py:

    venv/bin/python tools/mutants.py --exp exp_astro_insitu --tests tests/test_exp_astro_insitu.py --raw results/astro/insitu_raw.npz --md results/astro/insitu.md --out-env INSITU_OUT \\
        --spec tools/mutants/wp_astroinsitu_own.py --work <scratch dir> [--slot a --i0 0 --step 2]

A tuple is (id, what, old, new[, k]): `old` replaced by `new` at its k-th occurrence in experiments/exp_astro_insitu.py. The kill criterion is the tests file alone (the tests read nothing but the script, the
repository's src/ and experiments/ files, and, in the one test that regenerates the committed report, the raw and the md that the tool copies into the slot; the crowdsource test is skipped where the package is
not installed and a second test replaces the package by a recording stand-in, so that `run_cs3`'s arguments are tested in both environments). Ids: S the selection of stars, D detection and the constants, C the sky
and the aligned cut-outs, R the flux-weighted stack with outlier rejection, H the hybrid stamp, F the forward model of the centring, E the estimator, K collecting the stars, M the comparison statistics, B the
bootstrap and the held-out fit, V the validation part (stamps), W the raw and the --ref copy, G the guard and the runs, T Task B, P pooling and the statistics of the report, Q the report text, L the command line.

Result on the 93 tests of tests/test_exp_astro_insitu.py (the unmutated source passes the control with them and regenerates the md unchanged): 313 mutants, 297 killed, 16 survivors. Order of work: a first
complete pass on 60 tests left 88 survivors; the killable ones got a model-based test (an independent implementation of the clipped mean, the aligned cut-out, the stack, the forward model), boundary cases, or
a check of the wiring of `part_stamps`, `part_run`, `run_iss`, `part_cs_test` (93 tests now); the 88 were run again (72 killed). The 16 that remain change no output on any input the tests (or the data) can reach:
  C01  `<` for `<=` in the 3-sigma clip: the two differ only when a value lies exactly at 3 sigma of the current mean (measure zero);
  C05  stop at fewer than 4 instead of 3 survivors of the clip: a 3-sigma clip cannot leave fewer than 3 values (a sample of n values has |z| <= (n - 1) / sqrt(n), and it takes n >= 11 to clip at all);
  R04  the initial shape not normalised: the first update s = sum f c / sum f^2 is scale-invariant in s and is normalised afterwards;
  R15  f instead of f^2 in the denominator of the stack: a constant factor, removed by the normalisation that follows;
  R12  `<` for `<=` in the rejection test: differs only for a misfit exactly at the threshold;
  R10  the median of the misfit over all stars instead of the kept stars: differs only after a star was rejected, and moves the threshold by a few per cent, which no planted case or target patch crosses (NOT shown
       equivalent in general; left as a survivor);
  E04  the core not renormalised inside the fixed point: s_obs and the forward core both have sum 1 within 6 px, so the correction adds sum 0 (equal to rounding);
  M09  the truth sources of the box grown by 20 px instead of 0 for the truth stars: a truth star is more than 12 px from the edge and its neighbours within 4.5 px lie inside the box;
  M17  an unmatched star (index -1) not skipped in the isolation mask: it is compared with the last truth source and itself, and the self-comparison makes it not isolated, as the skip does;
  B06  resamples without an estimate not skipped in the bootstrap: `stat_vector` returns NaN for a NaN stamp, as the skip does;
  H12, H18  the shift axes of the held-out model, or its start, exchanged: a reparametrisation of the same least-squares problem, the fit returns the same minimum;
  V07  a patch with stored results computed again: the computation is deterministic and the raw is write-once with equal values;
  V17  the truth sources for the nearest-truth match from the box without the margin: a star more than 12 px from the edge has its nearest truth source within 1 px inside the box;
  W08  the hashes written at every save: the same values are written again;
  P03  baselines tested for the entry cap: they have no `bic` record, so the answer is the same.
"""
